o mal.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos junto al límite se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 48 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 15.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.1 to 4.5. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 23 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur naturally. The number of awardees does not prove wrongdoing. Legitimate reasons like market prices or budget constraints may explain the distribution.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and amounts for consistency. Verify if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review if the awardee A's contracts align with the body's needs. Contract [1] should be examined for its specific service and value.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["mqrCdKOfe3UmMOlAXxDEjw%3D%3D","PnFhq3Fk80JrhBlEHQFSKA%3D%3D","mG9pnsoc4zizz8fXU2i3eQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}